(2400346, 332238, 36328, '<td valign="top">This strong diagonal is very un-nerving. I understand what you were trying to do, but not sure it works here. A little too noisey, but I suspect that is due to the high ISO needed for the night shot. (2)</td>', 'This strong diagonal is very un-nerving. I understand what you were trying to do, but not sure it works here. A little too noisey, but I suspect that is due to the high ISO needed for the night shot. (2)', '2006-05-10 08:18:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(2400355, 332290, 36328, '<td valign="top">I wounder how many comments you''ll get saying ''too small''. I''d have to agree, I can''t see why you haven''t used the max 640px available to you. Is it the file size? Then reduce the quailty in Photoshop. Quality of between 60 and 90% is fine for DPC, but allows bigger images sizes. I suspect this would do well if it was bigger. (4) - sorry, needs to be bigger to see the image better.</td>', 'I wounder how many comments you''ll get saying ''too small''. I''d have to agree, I can''t see why you haven''t used the max 640px available to you. Is it the file size? Then reduce the quailty in Photoshop. Quality of between 60 and 90% is fine for DPC, but allows bigger images sizes. I suspect this would do well if it was bigger. (4) - sorry, needs to be bigger to see the image better.', '2006-05-10 08:22:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(2400357, 332471, 36328, '<td valign="top">Like the leading line, like the graphic look of this. Did you try this in B&amp;W? I reckon the stark contrast would make this stand out more. (6)</td>', 'Like the leading line, like the graphic look of this. Did you try this in B&W? I reckon the stark contrast would make this stand out more. (6)', '2006-05-10 08:24:42.000000', NULL, 1),
