(2438895, 331952, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Desert Nightlife" is an amazing entry into the Night Shot III challenge.  Top seven percent and 20th place, very well deserved.  Congratulations.<br/> <br/>The first thing that grabbed my attention was the colors, they are very beautiful for a night shot.  The clarity is very excellent especially with a long exposure shot.  The composition is prefect.  You have done wonderful work here. <br/> <br/>After reading your comments I am surprised this is not the desert.  The image defiantly looks like a prefect desert card.  I would be curious to see the original since you mentioned adjusting the temperature, but I am sure the blue/purple was much more of a night color. <br/> <br/>Again congrats and I look forward to your future entries.</td>', '*Critique Club* "Desert Nightlife" is an amazing entry into the Night Shot III challenge.  Top seven percent and 20th place, very well deserved.  Congratulations. The first thing that grabbed my attention was the colors, they are very beautiful for a night shot.  The clarity is very excellent especially with a long exposure shot.  The composition is prefect.  You have done wonderful work here.  After reading your comments I am surprised this is not the desert.  The image defiantly looks like a prefect desert card.  I would be curious to see the original since you mentioned adjusting the temperature, but I am sure the blue/purple was much more of a night color.  Again congrats and I look forward to your future entries.', '2006-05-20 01:33:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(2439178, 332356, 7252, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by rennie:</b></div><hr/><i>Suspicions hit you hard here. People didn''t believe it wasn''t processed within basic editing rules. Very undeserved score.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Huh? If people didn''t believe it wasn''t processed within basic editing rules then they would believe it was processed legally within basic editing. If that''s the case then there wouldn''t be any suspicions to "hit" anyone.</td>', 'Originally posted by rennie:Suspicions hit you hard here. People didn''t believe it wasn''t processed within basic editing rules. Very undeserved score.  Huh? If people didn''t believe it wasn''t processed within basic editing rules then they would believe it was processed legally within basic editing. If that''s the case then there wouldn''t be any suspicions to "hit" anyone.', '2006-05-20 02:58:13.000000', NULL, 0),
